---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const teardowns = (await getCollection('teardowns', ({ data }) => !data.draft)).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf()
);

const lost = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6];
const arrived = [7, 8, 9];
---

<Base
  title="Nomoro — Your signups don't become users"
  description="I find where people drop off between signing up and getting something out of your product. Then I rebuild that path and ship it. No deck."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <section class="pt-24 pb-32 sm:pt-40 sm:pb-48">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 452 36"
        class="mb-10 h-7 w-full max-w-sm sm:h-8"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Ten marks. Seven fade. Three remain."
      >
        {lost.map((i) => (
          <rect
            class="leak-mark lost"
            style={`--i: ${i}`}
            x={i * 47}
            y="0"
            width="24"
            height="36"
            rx="5"
          />
        ))}
        {arrived.map((i) => (
          <rect class="leak-mark" x={i * 47} y="0" width="24" height="36" rx="5" />
        ))}
      </svg>

      <h1 class="display measure">Your signups don't become users.</h1>
      <p class="lede measure mt-6" style="color: var(--ink-soft)">
        I find where people drop off between signing up and getting something out of your product.
        Then I rebuild that path and ship it. No deck.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#send">Send me a teardown of my onboarding</a>
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:jelle@nomoro.be?subject=Activation%20Diagnostic">Book the diagnostic, €4,500</a>
      </p>
      <p class="micro mt-8">
        Three years at Hootsuite on net-new user activation. Now doing it for smaller teams.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ The problem ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">The problem</p>
      <h2 class="headline measure mt-3">Seven in ten never get there.</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <p>
          At the product-led companies OpenView called best in class,
          <strong>20 to 30% of signups reached activation</strong>. Everyone else did worse. That
          is normal. It is not a sign your product is broken.
        </p>
        <p>
          You know your cost per signup. Ask which screen loses the most new users, and what that
          costs you a month, and <strong>most teams go quiet</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          You already paid to get those people in. They are inside your product right now, not
          finding a reason to stay. Fixing that needs no new budget, no new channel and no new
          features.
        </p>
        <p>
          It needs you to know where they go. That is
          <strong>a measurement problem before it is a design problem</strong>. I work in that
          order.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Who it is for ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">Who it is for</p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-8">
        <div>
          <h2 class="headline text-[1.25rem] sm:text-[1.375rem]">This is for you if</h2>
          <ul class="rows mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            <li>You are self-serve B2B SaaS, roughly €1M to €10M ARR</li>
            <li>People can sign up without talking to your sales team</li>
            <li>You get enough signups a month to measure a change</li>
            <li>
              There is a setup step before value. An integration, an import, an invite, a
              configuration
            </li>
            <li>
              Someone on your team owns an activation or retention number already, or is about to
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="headline text-[1.25rem] sm:text-[1.375rem]" style="color: var(--ink-soft)">
            This is not for you if
          </h2>
          <ul class="rows mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal" style="color: var(--ink-soft)">
            <li>Your product is sales-led and there is no self-serve path to fix</li>
            <li>
              You are pre-product-market-fit. Then the problem is the product, not the first run,
              and I would be taking your money
            </li>
            <li>
              You want design capacity instead of an answer. I am the wrong shape, and more
              expensive than the right one
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ How it works ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
      <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-8">
        <li>
          <span class="headline block text-[1.75rem]" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--ink-faint)">01</span>
          <h2 class="headline mt-2 text-[1.25rem]">Watch</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Real people using your product for the first time, next to whatever your data already
            tells you. Most teams have never sat through their own onboarding as a stranger would.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="headline block text-[1.75rem]" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--ink-faint)">02</span>
          <h2 class="headline mt-2 text-[1.25rem]">Locate</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Where people drop off, why, and what each drop costs you a month in euros. You get a
            leak map and a backlog, ranked by what each fix is worth instead of how easy it is.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="headline block text-[1.75rem]" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--ink-faint)">03</span>
          <h2 class="headline mt-2 text-[1.25rem]">Rebuild and ship</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Signup to first value, designed and built next to your engineers, and measured before
            it goes live.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ The offer ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">The offer</p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h2 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">Activation Diagnostic</h2>
          <p class="headline mt-3 text-[1.75rem]">€4,500</p>
          <p class="micro mt-1">Two weeks</p>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            We agree what activation means for your product. I read your funnel data, watch new
            signups use it, and take apart three onboardings like yours. You get the leak map, the
            monthly cost of the biggest drop, and a ranked backlog. Paid in full on signature.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">First Run Sprint</h2>
          <p class="headline mt-3 text-[1.75rem]">€18,000</p>
          <p class="micro mt-1">Six weeks, around three days a week</p>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            That pace lets your engineers build as we go instead of getting everything at the end.
            Signup to first value, rebuilt and shipped: setup flow, empty states, in-product
            guidance, the activation sequence. We agree the metric and the measurement window in
            writing before I start. One round of changes after it ships. 50% to begin, 50% on
            delivery.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">Activation Retainer</h2>
          <p class="headline mt-3 text-[1.75rem]">€6,000 <span class="text-[1rem]" style="color: var(--ink-soft)">a month</span></p>
          <p class="micro mt-1">Three months minimum</p>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Activation is a loop, not a fix. Hypothesis, design, ship, measure, repeat, with a
            monthly readout to whoever owns the number. Invoiced on the first, in advance.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="micro mt-6">
        All prices exclude VAT. Payment within 14 days. Anything outside the agreed scope gets
        quoted before it starts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Teardowns ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">Teardowns</p>
      <h2 class="headline measure mt-3">Watch me do it on someone else first.</h2>
      <p class="measure mt-5">
        Every week I take a product, sign up as a new user, and record where the first run breaks.
        No client relationship. Nothing softened. It is the same work the diagnostic starts with,
        so you may as well see it before you pay for it.
      </p>
      {
        teardowns.length > 0 && (
          <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {teardowns.map((t) => (
              <article>
                <video
                  class="w-full rounded-lg"
                  src={t.data.video}
                  poster={t.data.poster}
                  controls
                  preload="none"
                />
                <h3 class="headline mt-4 text-[1.125rem]">{t.data.title}</h3>
                <p class="micro mt-1">
                  {t.data.product} · {t.data.finding}
                </p>
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>
        )
      }
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Track record ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">Track record</p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-[13rem_1fr]">
        <img
          class="portrait w-44 sm:w-full sm:self-start"
          src="/jelle-eysermans-480.webp"
          srcset="/jelle-eysermans-480.webp 480w, /jelle-eysermans-960.webp 960w"
          sizes="(min-width: 640px) 13rem, 11rem"
          width="480"
          height="600"
          alt="Jelle Eysermans"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <dl class="grid content-start gap-x-8 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <dt class="headline text-[1.125rem]">Hootsuite</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Product Design Lead, three years. The objective was to raise DAU/MAU for net-new users.
            Onboarding journeys, in-product guidance, and the product metrics that defined the aha
            moment and told us whether we moved it.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="headline text-[1.125rem]">EY Studio+</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Head of Design. Rebuilt the design practice from 4 people to 10 in eight months.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="headline text-[1.125rem]">Onegrid</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Co-founder. A product taken from zero to one, including the part where you find out
            whether anyone wants it.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="headline text-[1.125rem]">Now</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Capitac, a Belgian investment platform. Before that Gemini Sports Analytics, whose
            product Sky Sports used for their World Cup talent analysis.
          </dd>
        </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="card mt-10 max-w-2xl">
        <p class="font-[610]">On numbers.</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
          I do not publish activation percentages I cannot source. Case studies from Nomoro work
          are being written now. They will name the client and say how we measured. Until then the
          teardowns above tell you more. Same work, someone else's product.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Close ============ -->
    <section id="send" class="pb-24 sm:pb-28">
      <h2 class="headline measure">Send me your product.</h2>
      <p class="measure mt-5">
        I will sign up as a new user, record what happens, and send you a short video. Where people
        drop off, and the two things I would change first. Free, and there is no pitch attached to
        it.
      </p>
      <form
        class="mt-9 max-w-xl"
        name="teardown"
        method="POST"
        action="/thanks"
        data-netlify="true"
        netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="teardown" />
        <p class="hidden">
          <label>Leave this empty: <input name="bot-field" /></label>
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <label class="micro mb-1.5 block" for="email">Email</label>
            <input class="field" type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="micro mb-1.5 block" for="product">Product URL</label>
            <input class="field" type="url" id="product" name="product" required placeholder="https://" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-3">
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Send me your product</button>
          <a class="micro underline underline-offset-2" href="mailto:jelle@nomoro.be?subject=Activation%20Diagnostic">
            Or book the diagnostic, €4,500
          </a>
        </div>
      </form>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
